-- title:
--   Ramified-prime Hecke idele: its lattice and commutation with the level
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q'$ be a prime such that $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order, i.e. it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and equals every order containing it. Let $N\neq 0$ be a natural number with $q'\nmid N$, and let $m$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ such that $m$ and $N\cdot m^{-1}$ both lie in [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) of $\Lambda_1$ (the additive group generated by $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adele), and such that the rational elements $h$ with $mhm^{-1}$ in that box form a maximal order. Let $R$ be this intersection $\Lambda_1\cap m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}$, of relative index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$ as additive subgroups. Let $\pi$ be a unit lying in `primeHeckeSet R q'`, so $\pi$ and $q'\cdot\pi^{-1}$ lie in the adelic box of $R$ while $\pi^{-1}$ and $q'^{-1}\cdot\pi$ do not, and assume the component of $\pi$ at every place $w$ with $q'\notin w$ is $1$. Then, first, a rational quaternion $h$ lies in [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele Λ₁ π`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) (the rational elements of $\pi\widehat{\Lambda_1}$) if and only if $h\in\Lambda_1$ and either $h=0$ or $\mathrm{padicValRat}\,q'(\mathrm{nrd}\,h)\geq 1$, where $\mathrm{nrd}\,h=h_{\mathrm{re}}^2-a\,h_{\mathrm{imI}}^2-b\,h_{\mathrm{imJ}}^2+ab\,h_{\mathrm{imK}}^2$; and second, for every unit $x$ one has [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele Λ₁ (x * π * m) = Submodule.ofFiniteIdele Λ₁ (x * m * π)`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19).
--
--   This records the local behaviour at the ramified prime $q'$ of the definite quaternion algebra: there the completion of the order is the unique maximal order of a division algebra, one-sided ideals are two-sided, and the Hecke-set conditions pin the reduced norm valuation of the $q'$-component of $\pi$ to $1$, so that $\pi\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ cuts out the prime above $q'$ and $\pi$ commutes with the level idele $m$ up to the lattice it defines. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison, in [`CerednikDrinfeld.ssFrobMatrixC_apply_eq_classSetHeckeMatrix_primeHeckeSet_of_forall_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.ssFrobMatrixC_apply_eq_classSetHeckeMatrix_primeHeckeSet_of_forall_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace), to match the Frobenius at $q'$ with the Hecke correspondence at $q'$ on the quaternionic class set.
